    "created_at": "2026-11-23T06:23:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-23T06:23:29Z",
    "body": "Done in part by commit `5721b0fff` (PR #3635): a tool that is too wide for a plain Slot is refused when the tool is assigned (create, `set_tool`, the UI links edit, a change of kind) and when a tool that a slot uses is made wider. The refusal names the two sizes. A Slot from the default takes the larger of 4 mm and the tool diameter as its width. The part for 2D Pocket (a warning at edit time) and the check of a later width edit are tracked in #3631. This issue closes; #3631 holds what remains.",
